# Never let a secret or a local artifact into the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.isnad/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.*
.venv/
.venv311/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
tests/
docs/
demo/
# ...except the recorded lab, which `/lab` imports and reads at runtime (R10).
# The merchant pilot and the fake operator stay out: they are development
# harnesses, and a runtime image has no business carrying a fake operator.
# Docker takes the LAST matching pattern, so the re-exclusion below still wins
# for bytecode caches.
!demo/__init__.py
!demo/lab/**
demo/lab/**/__pycache__/

# The registry signature is made with the DEPLOYMENT vault key, not the
# developer's. Shipping the dev .sig into an image makes a fresh volume — which
# generates its own key — refuse to start: the signature verifies against a key
# the new deployment does not trust. Sign at deploy time instead.
app/registry/*.sig
